{
  "_readme": [
    "The cards Tim is actively hunting. Drives /wanted.html and the Most Wanted",
    "band on the home page.",
    "",
    "Add an entry by naming the set and the card. `number` is what disambiguates:",
    "Mega Darkrai ex exists three times in Pitch Black (Ultra Rare #101, Special",
    "Illustration Rare #116, Mega Hyper Rare #120) and only the number says which",
    "one you mean. Run scripts/sync-wanted.mjs to attach the image, the TCGplayer",
    "link and the raw market price.",
    "",
    "PRICES. `raw` is filled in automatically from the set's own checklist under",
    "public/data/cards/, which is TCGplayer market prices via TCGdex and is the",
    "same figure /sets/, /cards.html and the Pokedex pages print for that card.",
    "It used to come from the Pokemon TCG API, which carries nothing at all for",
    "the newest sets, so four cards showed 'no market price yet' on a page whose",
    "own footnote explained that a set this new often has none, while every other",
    "page on the site was pricing all four. If a card really has no price",
    "anywhere, put one you have seen in `raw` and the site uses it; leave it null",
    "and the site omits the row rather than printing a zero.",
    "",
    "`psa10` is ALWAYS manual. No free API carries graded prices, so nothing can",
    "fetch it. Put in a number you have actually seen (PSA price guide, or eBay",
    "sold listings), set `psa10AsOf` to the date you checked, and `psa10Source`",
    "to where it came from. Leave it null and the site shows nothing rather than",
    "a made-up figure.",
    "",
    "`got` flips a card from hunting to caught, which is worth doing on camera."
  ],
